# fleet-roster.tsv — production OpenClaw agents reviewed by bin/fleet-review.sh
# and rendered on the public board by contrib/fleet-live/.
#
# Copy to config/fleet-roster.tsv and edit — that path is gitignored, so your
# agent names and role descriptions never land in a commit.
#
# Model is resolved at runtime from ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json (single source of
# truth); only the editorial fields live here.
#
# Columns (tab-separated). The first four are required, the last three are
# optional — omit them and every agent shows on the board with its role as the
# title.
#
#   agent    OpenClaw agent id, must match ~/.openclaw/agents/<id>/
#   team     free-form grouping, e.g. work / personal / internal
#   channel  where it is reachable, e.g. discord / telegram / internal
#   role     one-line mandate; text before an em dash is used as a short role
#   board    1 to show on the public fleet board, 0 to keep it off
#   title    short display title on the board card, e.g. "Content & SEO"
#   blurb    one-line description shown when a board card is expanded
#
# agent	team	channel	role	board	title	blurb
alex	work	discord	content & SEO — owns the blog end to end (research, draft, SEO pass, publish)	1	Content & SEO	Owns the blog pipeline end to end
robin	work	discord	design engineer — landing pages, UI builds, visual assets	1	Design Engineer	Landing pages, UI builds, visual craft
sam	work	discord	ops — outbound pipeline, support backstop, daily standup	1	Ops & Outreach	Pipelines, support backstop, standups
jules	work	discord	engineer — code-heavy project work and technical escalations	1	Engineer	Code-heavy work & technical escalations
iris	personal	telegram	chief of staff — inbox and calendar triage, morning brief, drafting	1	Chief of Staff	Inbox, calendar, morning brief, drafts
worker	internal	internal	execution worker — spawned for heavy build loops or when the plan is exhausted	0	Execution Worker	Spawned by other agents for heavy build loops
